1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,832
Hi everyone, I am Ujwal.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:05,765
Sunita's father is no more.

3
00:00:05,765 --> 00:00:09,747
What he left her is a tin of old papers: a passbook,

4
00:00:09,747 --> 00:00:12,733
an insurance bond, a share certificate.

5
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:14,096
The money is hers.

6
00:00:14,096 --> 00:00:17,252
The hard part is discovering where it is,

7
00:00:17,252 --> 00:00:18,792
and how to claim it.

8
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:20,846
This is Virasat.

9
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:24,346
Photograph the papers, and it finds the money,

10
00:00:24,346 --> 00:00:28,760
explains what to do in your language, and fills the forms.

11
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:33,068
Virasat turns each paper into structured fields,

12
00:00:33,068 --> 00:00:35,496
every one with its own confidence.

13
00:00:35,496 --> 00:00:39,579
Three forgotten papers become three places where money is

14
00:00:39,579 --> 00:00:40,152
waiting.

15
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:44,976
But Virasat can find something more important: the account

16
00:00:44,976 --> 00:00:46,740
that was never in the tin.

17
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:50,485
A legal heir can obtain the account holder's income tax

18
00:00:50,485 --> 00:00:51,166
statement.

19
00:00:51,166 --> 00:00:55,091
Virasat reads it for every bank and company that paid him,

20
00:00:55,091 --> 00:00:58,677
revealing accounts that never appeared in her papers.

21
00:00:58,678 --> 00:01:01,495
We are not just digitising what she found.

22
00:01:01,494 --> 00:01:04,512
We are helping her discover what was missing.

23
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,056
Real records are messy.

24
00:01:07,056 --> 00:01:10,365
Names appear differently across institutions,

25
00:01:10,365 --> 00:01:13,159
so when the full name is too specific,

26
00:01:13,159 --> 00:01:16,689
a broader search finds it: three years of unpaid

27
00:01:16,689 --> 00:01:17,424
dividends.

28
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:22,265
Three simple questions determine her route: nominee,

29
00:01:22,265 --> 00:01:23,875
legal heir, or court.

30
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:26,295
That decision is not made by AI.

31
00:01:26,295 --> 00:01:30,354
It comes from an open rule corpus: each institution's

32
00:01:30,354 --> 00:01:34,183
claim process, written down, versioned and tested,

33
00:01:34,183 --> 00:01:38,166
with the rule id shown so the decision is traceable.

34
00:01:38,166 --> 00:01:42,400
Then the documents she needs, and where to get each one.

35
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:47,905
Before Sunita acts, Virasat challenges its own guidance.

36
00:01:47,905 --> 00:01:52,117
One AI looks for problems, like this name mismatch.

37
00:01:52,117 --> 00:01:55,887
Another reviews it, and can only add caution,

38
00:01:55,887 --> 00:01:57,981
never override the rules.

39
00:01:57,981 --> 00:02:00,872
Sunita reads the reasoning herself.

40
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:04,990
Now everything becomes something she can use.

41
00:02:04,990 --> 00:02:08,475
One click creates her claim form, the checklist,

42
00:02:08,475 --> 00:02:11,306
and cover letters in English and Hindi.

43
00:02:11,306 --> 00:02:15,376
Virasat tracks it, and prepares the escalation if nobody

44
00:02:15,376 --> 00:02:17,048
replies in thirty days.

45
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:20,890
And it is not built only for people comfortable with

46
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,107
financial websites.

47
00:02:22,107 --> 00:02:24,231
The whole journey works in Hindi,

48
00:02:24,231 --> 00:02:27,577
and the guidance is read aloud for anyone who is not

49
00:02:27,577 --> 00:02:28,864
comfortable reading.

50
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,150
The economics work.

51
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:35,289
Serving one family costs about thirty six rupees of AI.

52
00:02:35,289 --> 00:02:39,482
The average returned at Gujarat's camps is thirty eight

53
00:02:39,482 --> 00:02:41,235
thousand seven hundred.

54
00:02:41,235 --> 00:02:45,599
And the Vault checks that today's accounts have nominees,

55
00:02:45,599 --> 00:02:49,580
so tomorrow's money does not become another family's

56
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:50,116
search.

57
00:02:50,115 --> 00:02:51,921
Find what was forgotten.

58
00:02:51,922 --> 00:02:53,427
Claim what is yours.

59
00:02:53,427 --> 00:02:54,029
Virasat.

60
00:02:54,029 --> 00:02:55,760
Your money, your right.

61
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,576
Thank you.
